# Keep the repository's text as it was written: LF, everywhere.
#
# The style test (test/style.test.mjs) asserts that every text file is LF and
# ends with one newline — and a checkout that turned its lines into CRLF,
# which is what git's core.autocrlf=true does by default on Windows, would
# fail it before the plugin's own tests even run. `eol=lf` is what holds that
# line on every platform: it applies even where core.autocrlf=true, so a
# Windows checkout sees the same bytes the repository stores and the style
# test reads the same text on every runner. CI runs the suite on Windows, so
# this file is load-bearing there, not cosmetic.
#
# The binary list is what keeps a format git cannot sniff correctly from
# being converted as if it were text.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly binary: never convert, never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.tgz binary
